{
  // ===========================================================================
  // tsconfig used by the Node SDK build to emit per-file `.d.ts` declarations
  // alongside tsup's JS output.
  //
  // Extends Fern's own emitted `tsconfig.json` verbatim — same `strict`,
  // `module: NodeNext`, `moduleResolution: NodeNext`, `target`, `include`,
  // `exclude` as the source-of-truth. The only override is the addition of
  // `emitDeclarationOnly: true`: tsup handles the JS emit, this pass produces
  // only the per-file `.d.ts` declarations. The `declaration: true` and
  // `outDir: ./dist` flags Fern already set carry through.
  //
  // This replaces tsup's `--dts` bundled output. The bundler (rollup-plugin-dts under the hood)
  // rewrites every top-level declaration to a synthetic `index_X` alias and re-exports them. That
  // rewrite breaks TypeScript's declaration merging: when a name has BOTH `interface X` AND
  // `declare namespace X { … }` at source level, the bundled barrel can only re-export ONE side,
  // so code that writes `Vectros.X` fails with TS2749 / TS2724. Per-file `.d.ts` next to the
  // source preserves the merge end to end: the source-level barrels (`export * from "./X.js"`)
  // are the canonical shape, and the consumer resolves through them naturally.
  // ===========================================================================
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true,
    // The full `tsc` type-check is intentional (no `noCheck`): it fails the build on dangling
    // generated files, such as a wrapper importing a type that the barrel no longer exports,
    // which tsup's lenient `--dts` bundling would ship silently.
    // Strip `.d.ts.map` emission: the generator's own tsconfig sets `declarationMap: true`, but
    // the maps reference source `.ts` paths outside `dist/`, and the package's
    // `files: ["dist", "README.md"]` does not ship the sources, so the maps would give broken
    // click-throughs. The declaration files already carry every signature and JSDoc.
    "declarationMap": false
  }
}
